In <28fccc$rd8@vixen.cso.uiuc.edu> mlandaue@ux4.cso.uiuc.edu (Michael C Landauer) writes:

>You have no food.  You're fainting.  You pray, but your god gets mad.
>No food nearby.  What can you do?  If you actually succeed in killing a monster
>while fainting, eating the corpse does no good because you faint again before
>eating enough to help you.

You could still take your chances, though. Firstly, this tends to
happen to low level characters most of the time, so a nasty bones
level may not be a big concern anyway. Secondly, you could  still
keep  going  and hope to kill something eventually that carries a
food ration.  Or  you  might  zap  unidentified  wands  at  small
corpses.  If  it's  a  wand of polymorph, the corpse may become a
food ration. Alternatively, if you zap a  wand  of  polymorph  at
yourself,  you  could turn into something that can eat stuff that
you cannot eat as a human. And go quaffing from fountains  --  it
may  not  help  much,  but it may still be enough to get you from
fainting to weak for your battle against the next monster.  Heck,
you may even get a chance to wish for loads of food rations...

